<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Launch Optimization Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    Organizations may struggle to optimize launches when performance
                    data is incomplete, customer feedback is not analyzed, or teams
                    focus on short-term activity instead of meaningful product outcomes.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Limited Launch Data:</b> Without reliable analytics, teams may
                    find it difficult to understand customer behavior and identify
                    areas that require improvement.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Low Product Adoption:</b> Customers may not immediately
                    understand the product or its value. Improving onboarding,
                    product education, and feature discovery can increase adoption.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Conversion Drop-Off:</b> Customers may abandon important
                    journeys because of unclear messaging, complicated workflows,
                    pricing concerns, or poor user experience.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Weak Channel Performance:</b> Some marketing or acquisition
                    channels may produce traffic but limited qualified customers.
                    Channel-level analysis helps organizations focus on higher-value
                    opportunities.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Inconsistent Messaging:</b> Different launch channels may
                    communicate different product benefits. Consistent positioning
                    helps customers understand the product more clearly.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Delayed Optimization:</b> Waiting until the end of a launch
                    to review results can cause teams to miss opportunities to correct
                    problems early.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Lack of Post-Launch Follow-Up:</b> Launch activity should
                    continue after release through customer engagement, feedback,
                    support, product education, and performance monitoring.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant launch challenges image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    ```

